---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import "@/styles/content.css";

/**
 * ⚠️ This document describes the site as it actually behaves TODAY: no
 * accounts, no analytics, no advertising, no network calls carrying user data.
 * That is an unusually strong claim and it is only true while it stays true.
 *
 * If analytics, an ad network, embedded video, or any third-party script is
 * ever added, this page MUST be updated in the same pull request. Under COPPA a
 * persistent identifier — an ad cookie, a device id, an analytics client id —
 * counts as personal information collected from a child, and shipping one while
 * this page says otherwise turns a technical change into a false statement.
 */
const title = "Privacy — School Skills";
const description =
  "School Skills collects nothing. No accounts, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking. Everything a child does stays in their own browser.";
const updated = "12 August 2026";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="page">
    <p class="page__eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>We don't collect anything</h1>
    <p class="page__lead">
      That is the whole policy. The rest of this page explains how that can be
      true, and what it means for you.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. There are no accounts, no sign-up, no email addresses, no
      analytics, no advertising, and no third-party scripts of any kind. We do
      not know who you are, how many of you there are, or that you visited.
    </p>

    <h2>How that's possible</h2>
    <p>
      School Skills is a static website. Every page is a file, served as-is —
      there is no application server, no database, and nothing for your child's
      answers to be sent to. When they finish a race, the result is written to
      your own browser's storage on your own device. It does not leave it.
    </p>

    <h2>What's stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Player profiles (a name you choose, an emoji, a colour and an age), and
      the history of races played: times, scores, and which facts were answered
      right or wrong. This is kept in your browser's IndexedDB storage.
    </p>
    <p>
      You control it completely. Clearing your browser's site data deletes all
      of it permanently, and deleting a player in the app removes that player
      and every race they ran. Because we never receive any of it, we cannot
      restore it — which is why the app offers a backup file you keep yourself.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is intended for children and the adults helping them. We do not
      knowingly collect personal information from anyone, of any age, because we
      do not collect personal information at all — including the persistent
      identifiers (advertising IDs, analytics IDs, tracking cookies) that
      children's privacy law treats as personal information.
    </p>
    <p>
      The name you type for a player is stored only in your browser. We suggest
      a first name or nickname; nothing checks it, and nothing transmits it.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We don't set any. There is no consent banner because there is nothing to
      consent to.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served from Amazon CloudFront. Like any web host, its servers
      process the standard request information needed to deliver a page — your
      IP address, browser type and the file requested — in short-lived
      operational logs. We do not use this to identify or track anyone, and it
      is never combined with anything from the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      There are no ads on this site today. If that ever changes, this page will
      be updated before any advertising code is added, and the change will be
      dated here.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      Last updated {updated}. Material changes will be reflected in that date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@schoolskills.app"
        >hello@schoolskills.app</a
      >
    </p>

    <footer class="page__foot">
      <a href="/">School Skills</a>
      <a href="/flash-cards">Flash cards</a>
      <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
